senses.gloss:
विश् (श, औ) विशति 6.
a. To enter.
With आ or प्र, to enter;
occupy; with उप, to sit down;
to approach; with नि to dwell;
with नि or अभिनि, to rest, sit
down, conceal; with निर् to go
out; with परि, to set before;
with सम्, to lie down; with
सन्नि, to be near or adjacent.

वि-शद (दः-दा-दं)
a. White; clear;
transparent; evident; beautiful.

वि-षय (यः) 1.
m. Worldly object;
possession; thing; object of
sense or of desire; sphere of
observation or action; country;
cluster of villages; resort; pro-
vincial peculiarity; ceremony;
husband.

वि-शसित (तः-ता-तं)
a. Hurt; killed;
cut up; well mannered.

वि-स्रब्ध (ब्धः-ब्धा-ब्धं)
a. Trusted;
placid; humble; steady.

वि-स्रम्भ (म्भः) 1.
m. Trust; affection;
acquaintance; killing.

विश्रयिन् (यी-यिणी-यि)
a. Living in;
depending on.

वि-स्रावण (णं) 1.
m. Making flow;
distilling; bleeding; rum.

वि-श्रुत (तः-ता-तं)
a. Famous, known;
dissolved; flowing; delighted.

विषया_यिन् (यी) 5.
m. A sensualist;
materialist; a king;
Kāmadeva;
an organ of sense.

विषाणिन् (णी) 5.
m. An elephant;
a bull; any animal with horns.

विष्किर (रः) 1.
m. A bird in general;
pulling to pieces.

विष्टम्भ (म्भः) 1.
m. Impediment;
stricture; paralysis; stopping;
placing.

वि-सर्ग (र्गः) 1.
m. Abandoning; gift;
riddance; voiding by stool; the
letter (ः); sun's southern course;
light, final emancipation.

वि-स्मय (यः) 1.
m. Wonder, surprise;
pride; doubt.

वि-स्मापन (नः) 1.
m. Deceit; illusion;
Kāma; astonishing.
